    <heading level="1">Technology</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, graph the polynomial functions using a calculator. Based on the graph, determine the intercepts and the end behavior.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="51" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$f(x) = x^{3}(x - 2)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>The $$y- y-$$ intercept is $$( 0, 0 ). ( 0, 0 ).$$ The $$x- x-$$ intercepts are $$( 0, 0 ),( 2, 0 ). ( 0, 0 ),( 2, 0 ).$$ As $$x\to -\infty x\to -\infty$$ , $$f(x)\to \infty ,asx\to \infty ,f(x)\to \infty f(x)\to \infty ,asx\to \infty ,f(x)\to \infty$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
